sult", "type": "PE_RESULT", "localized_name": "pe_result"}, {"widget": {"name": "resolution"}, "name": "resolution", "label": "resolution", "type": "INT", "localized_name": "resolution"}, {"widget": {"name": "follow_input_size"}, "name": "follow_input_size", "label": "follow_input_size", "type": "BOOLEAN", "localized_name": "follow_input_size"}], "flags": {}, "id": 2, "type": "QwenPECanvasT8", "title": "Qwen Image 2.1 PE Canvas", "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {"follow_input_size": true, "resolution": true}, "Node name for S&R": "QwenPECanvasT8"}, "order": 8}, {"outputs": [], "color": "#432", "widgets_values": ["## Qwen Image 2.1 · 文生图（已优化）\n\n**运行顺序**：先跑 `Qwen Image 2.1 PE Rewrite ` 把中文/大白话改写成专业提示词，\n再交给 Qwen Image 2.1 出图。\n\n**本次优化**\n- 新增 `Qwen Image 2.1 Cache`，KV 缓存压到 **int8** → 12G 显存也能稳跑（原来容易爆显存）。\n- `cfg = 1`、`euler + simple`：官方推荐路径。**只有填了负面提示词才需要把 cfg 调到 2~4。**\n- 步数默认 25。显存/时间紧张可降到 12~15；追求质量升到 40~50。\n\n**尺寸**：`Qwen Image 2.1 PE Canvas ` 会按改写结果给出比例。\n原生支持 2K，但 12G 显存跑 2048 会非常慢，建议先用 1024 档。\n\n**透明背景**：把 PE 节点的 `transparent_rgba` 打开，或让提示词以\n`This is an RGBA format image with transparency.` 开头，并以 PNG 保存。\n\n**模型位置**\n- `models/diffusion_models/qwen_image_2.1_int8_convrot.safetensors`\n- `models/text_encoders/qwen3vl_8b_int8_convrot.safetensors`\n- `models/vae/qwen_image_2.1_vae_bf16.safetensors`\n- `models/llm/qwenimage-pe/` 放 PE 改写模型的 GGUF\n"], "inputs": [], "flags": {}, "type": "MarkdownNote", "title": "使用说明 / 优化点", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#653", "size": [430, 340], "pos": [-120, 220], "id": 101, "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}}, "order": 3}, {"mode": 0, "outputs": [{"name": "rewritten_prompt", "links": [1, 4], "label": "rewritten_prompt", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "rewritten_prompt"}, {"name": "pe_result", "links": [2], "label": "pe_result", "type": "PE_RESULT", "localized_name": "pe_result"}, {"name": "diagnostics", "links": [3], "label": "diagnostics", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "diagnostics"}], "size": [480, 590], "pos": [342.4867248535156, 268.0849609375], "widgets_values": ["A vertically framed realistic photograph shows a young tabby kitten sitting indoors beside a bright sunlit window. The composition places the kitten slightly right of center in the foreground, occupying most of the middle and lower portions of the image. Its full body is visible from head to curled tail, though the head dominates due to the close perspective. The kitten has short gray-beige tabby fur with dark charcoal stripes across the forehead, cheeks, shoulders, legs, and tail. Its coat appears plush and fine-textured, with warmer tan highlights where sunlight catches individual hairs. The kitten’s large round eyes are wide open and directed outward through the glass, giving it a curious, attentive expression. Its head tilts gently downward and slightly sideways, emphasizing a playful, contemplative pose. The ears are tall triangular shapes with translucent pink inner skin and delicate pale fur along their rims, especially illuminated by backlighting. The nose is small and pink, the muzzle is light cream-white, long white whiskers extend prominently from both sides of the snout, and the mouth area remains relaxed rather than open. One front leg rests forward over the padded surface, showing rounded toes and darker striping, while the other foreleg angles inward under the chest. A ringed tail curves near the lower center-left area of the cat’s body. Behind and around the kitten, warm daylight streams through the window from the right and rear, producing a golden rim-light effect on the ears, cheek fur, shoulder, and whiskers.\n\nThe window spans nearly the full height of the image and sits directly behind and to the right of the kitten. Several vertical wooden or honey-toned window-frame strips divide the glass panels, including narrow bands near the upper center-left and midsection. Outside the window, the view is intentionally blurred with shallow depth of field: blue patches of sky and cloud occupy much of the background, while dense green tree foliage fills the lower half and right side. On the far right exterior area, part of a neighboring residential building façade is visible, rendered softly out of focus; it includes pale walls, rectangular window openings, balcony-like forms, and reddish roof tiles along the top portion. Near the left-middle background, clusters of purple flowering plants appear among deep green leaves, also heavily defocused. These botanical elements create colorful bokeh circles and soften the otherwise bright urban-garden backdrop.\n\nAt the top-right quadrant, partially lowered horizontal blinds cover the upper section of the glass panel. The blinds consist of many thin metallic or painted slats stacked diagonally within perspective, colored muted bronze-gray with dark shadow gaps between them. They run horizontally across the window, overlapping visually with the blurred sky and exterior architecture. Along the far right edge hangs a sheer lace curtain made of off-white fabric. The curtain falls vertically with scalloped trim near the lower visible edge and carries subtle floral embroidery or appliqué patterns in dusty mauve-pink thread. Some blossoms and vine motifs overlap the kitten’s silhouette and nearby window reflections, creating layered texture. Soft folds cast faint shadows down the curtain, suggesting lightweight textile material.\n\nOn the far left background, another slender houseplant rises against a plain beige wall. It has multiple thin stems and elongated green leaves extending into the frame from the left margin, positioned behind the kitten and further blurred by the lens. The wall itself is smooth, matte, and neutral taupe-gray, providing a calm interior backdrop. The windowsill and seating surface beneath the kitten look upholstered or cushioned, covered in a pale woven fabric matching the warm, textured palette of the room. In the lower-left to central lower area, a wicker or rattan basket peeks into view. Inside or just adjacent to the basket lies a loosely wound ball of thick woolen yarn in soft pastel strands, mainly lavender-purple with hints of salmon orange, coral, beige, and yellow-orange. The yarn fibers look fuzzy and handcrafted, contrasting with the hard smoothness of the window glass and glossy architectural lines outdoors. At the extreme bottom-left corner, only part of a decorative ceramic bowl, mug, or planter is visible, cropped by the image border. It has an earthy speckled base color with painterly ornamental patterning, possibly containing soil or waterless plant matter, reinforcing the handmade home-decor theme.\n\nThe photograph uses a close-up lifestyle approach with shallow depth of field: the kitten is sharply focused, particularly the face, eye regions, ear interiors, whiskers, and fur pattern, while the garden, buildings, curtain edge, and foreground objects fall into progressively softer blur. Lighting is natural and directional, strongest from the right and rear, causing high brightness on the glass and luminous outlines on the cat’s fur while maintaining gentle shadow detail on the left-facing side. The overall color grading leans warm, cinematic, and pastoral, combining creamy whites, leafy greens, weathered browns, muted grays, and sun-dappled golds. The visual mood suggests a quiet daytime moment inside a cozy apartment overlooking greenery.", "t2i", "1:1", "English", false, "Qwen-Image-2.1-PE-T2I.Q4_K_M.gguf", "Qwen-Image-2.1-PE-I2I.Q4_K_M.gguf", "Auto", "after_run", 42, "fixed"], "inputs": [{"shape": 7, "name": "image_1", "label": "image_1", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "image_1"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "image_2", "label": "image_2", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "image_2"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "image_3", "label": "image_3", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "image_3"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "image_4", "label": "image_4", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "image_4"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "image_5", "label": "image_5", "type